---
description: Recurring corrections from code review — avoid repeating these mistakes
alwaysApply: true
---

- Rate limiter tests must use MemoryStore directly, not RedisStore + ioredis-mock. rate-limit-redis's sendCommand bridge (redisClient.call) is not implemented by ioredis-mock and will break module load.
- Integration tests for routes that have rate limiting applied must mock createRateLimiter as a pass-through middleware. Rate limiting behavior has its own dedicated test file (tests/middleware/rateLimiter.test.ts) — don't couple route logic tests to rate limiting internals.
- Config tests that need to simulate a "missing" env var must set it to an empty string, not delete it from process.env. Deleting lets dotenv's file-based .env values repopulate the key during isolateModules re-imports, silently defeating the test.
- Regex character classes: never write a class ending in \\- (matches a literal backslash followed by a literal hyphen). A literal hyphen inside a character class must be unescaped and placed at the start or end of the class, e.g. [a-z0-9_.-].
- Login schema (loginSchema.ts) deliberately omits username format and password complexity validation present in registration. This is intentional for enumeration protection (a malformed-input error and a wrong-credentials error must look identical), not an oversight — do not add complexity/format validation to login.
- loginService's dummy-hash timing mitigation (DUMMY_HASH) must remain a real, valid Argon2id hash verified before the not-found rejection. Do not remove, shortcut, or make this call conditional — its purpose is making response timing identical for nonexistent-username and wrong-password cases.
- Rate limiting must always go through the shared createRateLimiter factory (src/middleware/rateLimiter.ts). Limit-exceeded responses route through next(new RateLimitedError()) so they use the standard error envelope — never write a custom 429 response body.